 use.\")\nCovers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008012 (quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008012 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that is mitotically quiescent.  These cells are wedge shaped and have a large nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio with few organelles, a small nucleus and condensed interphase chromatin. Satellite cells typically remain in this state until activated following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008012 \"quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008023 (obsolete cardiac fibroblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008023 \"obsolete cardiac fibroblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009078 (thymic fibroblast type 1)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009078 \"A fibroblast located in the thymic capsule.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009078 \"thymic capsular fibroblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009078 \"thymic fibroblast type 1\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009079 (thymic fibroblast type 2)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009079 \"A fibroblast located between thymic lobules.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009079 \"thymic interlobular fibroblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009079 \"thymic fibroblast type 2\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081841\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22045730\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24605102\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009099 \"A progenitor cell that is a tissue-resident mesenchymal cell, important for skeletal muscle regeneration, and able to differentiate into both adipocytes or fibroblasts.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009100 (hepatic portal fibroblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20209607\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24814904\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009100 \"A fibroblast located in the portal triad. Hepatic portal fibroblast are a non-parenchymal cell population located adjacent to bile duct epithelia in liver and are distinct from stellate cells. They differentiate into fibrogenic myofibroblasts during chronic injury states producing high levels of collagen.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0009100 \"portal fibroblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009100 \"hepatic portal fibroblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009101 (fibroblastic reticular cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009101 \"fibroblastic reticular cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009102 (lymph node fibroblastic reticular cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009102 \"A specialized, fibroblastic reticular cell of mesenchymal origin found in lymph nodes. In human, it expresses several markers common to myofibroblasts (desmin, vimentin, CD73, CD90, α-smooth muscle actin (αSMA)), and can be differentiated from endothelial cells by its lack of CD31 expression. These cells are critical for the overall organization and function of the lymph node. Lymph node fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) can be further classified based on their location, function, and unique marker expression.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0009102 \"fibroblastic reticular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009102 \"lymph node fibroblastic reticular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009103 \"A fibroblastic reticular cell found in the lymph node subcapsular sinus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009104 \"A fibroblastic reticular cell found in the lymph node germinal center dark zone (B cell zone).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009104 \"lymph node germinal center dark zone fibroblastic reticular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009105 \"A fibroblastic reticular cell found in the lymph node T cell domain.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009105 \"lymph node T cell domain fibroblastic reticular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasD