{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'PATO_0000380|PATO_0000381|quiescent|activated|cellular quiescence|cell quiescence|GO_0044838|GO_0008283|GO_0007049|has_quality|RO_0000086' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"3706:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000001 \"Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n3718:Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n3784:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000010 \"Note that this class was re-labeled to 'cultured cell' instead of 'cell line cell', as it intent was clarified to cover any cultured cells of multicellular and unicellular organisms. This includes cells actively being cultured, or cells that have been cultured but are stored in a quiescent state for future use. In having been cultured, cells must establish homeostasis and often replicate in a foreign environment. Accomodation of this stress initiates a selection of cells fit for such challenges, wherein necessary adaptive biochemical and.or genetic changes can occur. These changes can set them apart from the in vivo cells from which they derive, and such changes will typically accumulate and change over increasing time in culture.\")\n5919:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000229 \"Refers to an activated mature lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'lymphocyte ; CL:0000542' or one of its children instead.\")\n5926:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000230 \"Refers to an activated mature T lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'T cell ; CL:0000084' or one of its children instead.\")\n5933:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000231 \"Refers to an activated mature B lymphocyte phenotype rather than a distinct cell type; consider using 'B cell ; CL:0000236' or one of its children instead.\")\n5959:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000233 \"Platelets are reportedly CCR1-positive, CCR2-negative, CCR3-positive, CCR4-positive, CCR5-negative, CCR6-negative, CCR7-negative, CCR8-negative, CCR9-negative, CCR10-negative, CD16-positive, CD23-positive, CD32-positive, CD40-positive, CD41-positive CD42-positive, CD61-positive, CD62P-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD102-positive, CD147-positive (activated platelets), CD154-positive (activated platelets), CD162-positive, CD209, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD181-negative, CD182-negative, CD183-negative, CD184-positive, CLEC2-positive, GPVI-positive, JAMC-positive, PAR1-positive, PAR2-negative, PAR3-positive, PAR4-positive, TSP1-positive, and TXA2R-positive. Platelets can reportedly produce CCL2, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL17, CD40L, CXCL1, CXCL4, CXCL4L1, CXCL5, CXCL7, CXCL8, CXCL12, EGF, factor V, factor VII, factor XI, factor XIII, bFGF, histamine, IGF-1, IL-1beta, PAI-1, PDGF, plasminogen, protein S, serotonin, TGF-beta, TFPI, VEGF, and vWF.\")\n8852:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D032496\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000594 \"An elongated, spindle-shaped, cell that is located between the basal lamina and the plasmalemma of a muscle fiber. These cells are mostly quiescent, but upon activation they divide to produce cells that generate new muscle fibers.\")\n9184:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12808230\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17239632\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18222966\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9302568\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatic_stellate_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000632 \"A cell that is found in the perisinusoidal space of the liver that is capable of multiple roles including storage of retinol, presentation of antigen to T cells (including CD1d-restricted NKT cells), and upon activation, production of extracellular matrix components that can contribute to liver fibrosis. This activated state has a myofibroblast-like phenotype, though it's not clear in the literature if this is terminally differentiated. This cell type comprises approximately 8-15% of total cells in the liver.\")\n10568:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000785 \"A B cell that is mature, having left the bone marrow. Initially, these cells are IgM-positive and IgD-positive, and they can be activated by antigen.\")\n10601:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081059\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_B_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000787 \"A memory B cell is a mature B cell that is long-lived, readily activated upon re-encounter of its antigenic determinant, and has been selected for expression of higher affinity immunoglobulin. This cell type has the phenotype CD19-positive, CD20-positive, MHC Class II-positive, and CD138-negative.\")\n10612:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781765196\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19447676\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081059\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20933013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000788 \"A naive B cell is a mature B cell that has the phenotype surface IgD-positive, surface IgM-positive, CD20-positive, CD27-negative and that has not yet been activated by antigen in the periphery.\")\n11105:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14685782\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000824 \"lymphokine activated killer cell\")\n11507:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000863 \"classically activated macrophage\")\n11723:# Class: obo:CL_0000890 (alternatively activated macrophage)\n11728:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000890 \"alternatively activated macrophage\")\n11795:# Class: obo:CL_0000896 (activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell)\n11797:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000896 \"A recently activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell with the phenotype CD69-positive, CD62L-negative, CD127-negative, and CD25-positive.\")\n11798:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000896 \"activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T lymphocyte\")\n11799:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000896 \"activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T-cell\")\n11800:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000896 \"activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T-lymphocyte\")\n11801:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000896 \"activated CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell\")\n11936:# Class: obo:CL_0000906 (activated CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell)\n11939:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000906 \"activated CD8-positive, alpha-beta T lymphocyte\")\n11940:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000906 \"activated CD8-positive, alpha-beta T-cell\")\n11941:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000906 \"activated CD8-positive, alpha-beta 