{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '22760,22815p' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"\n# Class: obo:CL_0008010 (cranial somatomotor neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14699587\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008010 \"A cranial motor neuron whose soma is located in the midbrain andor hindbrain and which innervates the skeletal muscles of the eye or tongue.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008010 \"cranial somatomotor neuron\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008010 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0015000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002120 obo:CL_0008002)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008011 (skeletal muscle satellite stem cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008011 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that divides by stem cell division.  A proportion of this population undergoes symmetric stem cell division, producing two skeletal muscle satellite stem cells. The rest undergo asymmetric stem cell division - retaining their identity while budding off a daughter cell that differentiates into an adult skeletal muscle myoblast.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008011 \"skeletal muscle satellite stem cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008011 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000594 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001400) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0017145)))\nDisjointClasses(obo:CL_0008011 obo:CL_0008020)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008012 (quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008012 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that is mitotically quiescent.  These cells are wedge shaped and have a large nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio with few organelles, a small nucleus and condensed interphase chromatin. Satellite cells typically remain in this state until activated following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008012 \"quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0008012 obo:CL_0000594)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008013 (cranial visceromotor neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14699587\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008013 \"A visceromotor motor neuron whose soma is located in the hindbrain, and which synapses to parasympathetic neurons that innervate tear glands, sweat glands, and the smooth muscles of the head.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008013 \"cranial visceromotor neuron\"@en)\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008013 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0005025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002028)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0008013 obo:CL_0015000)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008014 (obsolete excitatory motor neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008014 \"A motor neuron that is capable of directly inducing muscle contraction.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008014 \"In vertebrates, all motor neurons are excitatory, but various types of inhibitory motor neurons exist in invertebrates.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008014 \"obsolete excitatory motor neuron\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0008014 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008015 (inhibitory motor neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008015 \"A motor neuron that is capable of directly inhibiting muscle contraction.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0008015 obo:NCBITaxon_7742)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008015 \"In vertebrates, all motor neurons are excitatory, but various types of inhibitory motor neurons exist in invertebrates.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008015 \"inhibitory motor neuron\"@en)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0008015 obo:CL_0000100)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008016 (activated skeletal muscle satellite cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008016 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that has become mitotically active - typically following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008016 \"activated skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0008016 obo:CL_0000594)\nSubClassOf(Annotation(rdfs:comment \"More accurately - transformation_of ?\") obo:CL_0008016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0008012))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0008017 (adult skeletal muscle myoblast)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008017 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that is part of a skeletal mucle.  These cells are formed following acivation and division of skeletal muscle satellite cells. They form a transient population that is lost when they fuse to form skeletal muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0008017 \"myogenic precursor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008017 \"The vast majority of these cells develop from skeletal muscle satellite cells, although there are some reports of other origins.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008017 \"adult skeletal muscle myoblast\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008017 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001134) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0008002)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
